Riftway CEF patch 0009: the browser process's accessibility mode.

Adds the static CefBrowserHost::GetProcessAccessibilityMode and
SetProcessAccessibilityMode (cef_browser_host_get_process_accessibility_mode,
cef_browser_host_set_process_accessibility_mode) and
CefBrowserProcessHandler::OnAccessibilityModeChanged, as Electron's
app.isAccessibilitySupportEnabled, get/setAccessibilitySupportFeatures,
setAccessibilitySupportEnabled and accessibility-support-changed use
content::BrowserAccessibilityState: the getter reads the process's effective
ui::AXMode flags, the setter keeps one ScopedAccessibilityMode for the process
(Electron's scoped_accessibility_mode_), replaced by the next call, and the
callback reports the flags Chromium adds by itself (a ui::AXModeObserver on
ui::AXPlatform: an assistive technology using the platform APIs), not those
the setter adds. Chromium has no observer for removed flags. CefContext owns
the state from context initialisation to shutdown. API at CEF_NEXT (999998):
API version 15400 and its hash are unchanged.

Resolves: Riftway docs/DRIFT.md A28.
Base: CEF a03e714 (branch 8037, CEF 154) with 0001-0008. Applies in chromium/src/cef.

